E=[('Redline 15 · the Church\'s teaching under the three movements', 128,
 'and in each of them, truth, justice, mercy and sacrifice are doing the quiet work.',
 'and in each of them, truth, justice, mercy and sacrifice are doing the quiet work. That is no accident. As we saw in Chapter 5, on how love binds every virtue together, the Church calls charity "the form of the virtues" (*CCC* 1827). Prudence is not a second rule standing beside love; it is love doing its thinking.'),
 ('Redline 15 · command as self-gift', 136,
 'it acts, and the acting will cost something. That cost is **sacrifice**: love at last poured out in deed.',
 'it acts, and in acting it gives itself. That self-gift is **sacrifice**: love at last poured out in deed.')]
